@startuml crossexam-states
' What a claim's state can become in --mode crossexam.
' Traced against src/afriend/verdicts.py (state_for,
' should_discard, build_successor) and spec §7.1-§7.2.

' Theme: colours sampled from docs/images/brand/afriend-logo-512.png.
' Avenir Next and SF Mono ship with macOS and are absent from the CI runner,
' which only checks that a source renders -- the committed PNG and SVG pair
' is produced by `make diagrams` on a machine that has them.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "Avenir Next"
skinparam defaultMonospacedFontName "SF Mono"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #6E8288
skinparam ArrowFontColor #5B7079
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 19
skinparam TitleFontColor #2D424E
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F8FCFC
skinparam legendBorderColor #A8C3CC
skinparam legendFontSize 12
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F4F1E8
skinparam noteBorderColor #B3AA97
skinparam noteFontColor #4A4436
skinparam noteFontSize 12
skinparam StateBorderColor #7E99A3
skinparam StateBackgroundColor #EAF3F4
skinparam StateFontColor #2D424E
skinparam StateFontSize 13
skinparam StateAttributeFontSize 12

title Claim states in cross-examination

legend top right
  <color:#7A9B72>██</color>  terminal, clears a gate
  <color:#C07A6E>██</color>  terminal, needs a human
  <color:#7E99A3>██</color>  another round could change it
endlegend

state "contested" as C
state "settled-upheld" as SU #F3D7D2
state "settled-refuted" as SR #D9E8D5
state "superseded" as SUP #D9E8D5
state "deadlocked" as DL #F3D7D2
state "unproven" as UP
state "incomplete" as IN
state "discarded" as DIS #D9E8D5

[*] --> C : round 1 raised it

C --> SU : judges unanimously\n**upheld**
C --> SR : judges unanimously\n**refuted**
C --> SUP : judges unanimously\n**amended**
C --> C : rounds remain
C --> DL : judges disagree,\nno rounds left
C --> UP : below quorum
C --> IN : below quorum: a\nrequired judge is missing

UP --> C : a judge changed its mind
UP --> DIS : same verdict set from\nworking judges, two rounds running
IN --> C : the missing judge reported

SUP --> [*] : successor **c-NNNN@2**\nenters the next round as *contested*

note bottom of SU
  Not a pass. The judges agreed
  the defect is real, so a gate
  needs a Resolution, not silence.
end note

note bottom of DL
  Never resolved by majority.
  Both sides are quoted verbatim
  and the call is the reader's.
end note

note right of UP
  A dispositive verdict whose judge
  could not locate the evidence is
  downgraded to unproven first (§6.5),
  so nobody settles a claim by not
  having looked.

  A sandbox access failure instead
  leaves the claim incomplete: it was
  not assessed, and cannot discard it.
end note

@enduml
